WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.550
Case storage should be predictable, access controlled, and protected against loss.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.970
Keep active material in approved local or organizational locations rather than scattered

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:09.360
downloads,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.880
browser folders, personal cloud accounts, and removable drives.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.840
Encrypted storage helps protect case material if a device or drive is lost or accessed

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.945
improperly.

00:00:17.945 --> 00:00:21.320
Encryption depends on strong authentication and recoverable key management.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.505
It does not replace least privilege, secure sharing, endpoint protection, or backups.

00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:29.865
Use a backup strategy that covers notes, source logs, preserved evidence, configuration,

00:00:29.865 --> 00:00:32.425
and final reports according to policy.

00:00:32.425 --> 00:00:34.810
Maintain more than one protected copy when risk warrants it,

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.005
and avoid treating virtual-machine snapshots or sync alone as a complete backup.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:39.987
Test restoration.

00:00:39.987 --> 00:00:42.985
A successful backup job does not prove that files, permissions, keys,

00:00:42.985 --> 00:00:45.075
and case structure can be recovered.

00:00:45.075 --> 00:00:48.670
Periodic restore exercises should verify integrity, document recovery steps,

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.645
and identify who is responsible during device failure.

00:00:51.645 --> 00:00:55.210
Retention policies define how long each category of material remains.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.020
Some cases require preserved records;

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.115
others require prompt cleanup of unnecessary personal data.

00:01:00.115 --> 00:01:03.240
Apply legal holds and organizational schedules where applicable,

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.120
then delete expired material through approved methods.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.315
Audit trails should record significant access, exports, transfers, retention changes,

00:01:10.315 --> 00:01:12.795
and deletion when the risk requires it.

00:01:12.795 --> 00:01:16.435
Protect backups and exported reports to the same standard as active data.

00:01:16.435 --> 00:01:20.350
Storage discipline keeps evidence available for legitimate review without creating an

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.700
indefinite archive of sensitive public information.
